  ],
  "misconceptions": [
    {
      "belief": "A rate limiter protects a service from a flood of traffic.",
      "correction": "It protects fairness between well-behaved clients. A real flood of 2 million requests per second still reaches the gateways, which must parse every request and look up its key before refusing; dropping that traffic belongs to the network edge.",
